  "articleBody": "Getting new countertops is exciting, but there are a few common pitfalls you'll want to steer clear of to ensure a smooth process and a beautiful result. First, don’t overlook confirming that your existing cabinets can actually support the weight of your new countertops, especially if you’re upgrading to a heavier material like granite or quartz. Another big one is not thinking about clearances for appliances or ensuring overhangs are correct – you don't want a dishwasher that can't open properly! Make sure you double-check where your sink and faucet cutouts will be placed before fabrication to avoid any surprises. Homeowners often forget to prepare their space by clearing out cabinets, protecting floors, and removing valuables. Doing these simple steps beforehand makes the installation day much smoother for everyone. And definitely don't let anyone skip the final fit and finish checks; you want those seams to be tight and the edges perfect. If you're unsure about any of these steps, that's when calling in professionals like HH Remodeling really makes a difference. We handle all these details for our clients in the Denver area, making sure your new countertops are installed flawlessly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}